	Select several with J, K or v, then x completes them all and gG groups them.
	Add a block with o below, O above, i or I inside, or a or A at the end or start of the list; for a section, project, task or note there, find New Section Below and the like with Ctrl+P.
	Make a line of text a section with S, and plain text again with s.
	Color a block with c1 to c6, red to violet, cycle colors with cc, pick one with mc, and remove it with C.
	While editing, start a line with - and a space for a task or end it with : for a project, and Backspace at its start or Delete at its end makes it text again.
	While editing, type / for this block's commands and filter them as you type, as in /due or /color, then Enter.
	Open Today with gt for what is due or started by today; gz or . on one of its blocks goes to it in the outline.
	Press G for the last block and gg for the first: the block focus lands on flashes, and z flashes what an undo brings back. Turn this down with Animations in the settings.
	In a truecolor theme such as Nord, complete a task with x and its text eases into the done style, zoom in with . and the outline fades in from the top, and themes crossfade as you move through them.
	Jump to any block by name with Ctrl+K, or to a project with gP; Alt+Enter or Ctrl+V there opens it in a new pane.
	Press Ctrl+G for the Navigator, a window of Today, your bookmarks and projects: type to filter it, ↑, ↓ and Enter go to one, and Ctrl+G or Esc closes it.
	Move between the panes with Ctrl+Shift+← and Ctrl+Shift+→, or Ctrl+W ← and Ctrl+W →.
	Find any command by name with Ctrl+P or :, such as Count Blocks and Words for what is under the focused block, or Save As to keep this file somewhere of your own.
	Press g, for the settings: theme, icons, word wrap, animations, autosave delay and backups, each kept in ~/.config/taskpaper-terminal/config.toml as you change it.
	Icons need a Nerd Font: if they show as boxes, press g, and set Icons to none with l.
	The mouse works too: click a block, the ▸ of a folded one to unfold it, a crumb or a Navigator entry, Alt+click to open it in a new pane, right-click for its menu.
	Change the colors with Ctrl+P and Choose Theme: each theme shows as you move to it, Enter keeps it and Esc goes back.
Packing list template:
